' SIS #02 — your FINAL sequence diagram goes here, as PlantUML (@startuml … @enduml).
' Start from the AI's original in models/original/sequence.puml, apply your accepted review
' decisions, then render it to models/img/sequence.png (or .svg). README section 5.
@startuml
title Course Registration — browse, guarded success, full and duplicate outcomes
autonumber

actor Student as S
participant "Catalog View" as UI
participant "Registration Service" as RS
entity "CourseOffering" as CO
entity "Enrollment" as EN

== US-01: Browse offerings (R1, AC-01) ==
S -> UI : view catalog(semester)
activate UI
UI -> CO : query offerings(semester)
activate CO
CO --> UI : offerings with courseCode, title,\nofferingId, availablePlaces
deactivate CO
UI --> S : catalog listing(courseCode, title,\nofferingId, availablePlaces)
deactivate UI
note over S, CO
  AC-02 (R2): browsing reserves nothing.
  availablePlaces is a derived value,
  rechecked only at registration time.
end note

== US-02 / US-03: Request registration (R2–R5) ==
S -> RS : register(student, offeringId)
activate RS
RS -> CO : checkAndEnroll(student, offeringId)  «one transaction»
activate CO

group atomic transaction - final checks and creation are one step
  CO -> EN : findEnrollment(student, offeringId)
  activate EN
  EN --> CO : existing | none
  deactivate EN
  alt already enrolled
    CO --> RS : REJECTED("already enrolled")
    RS --> S : rejection "already enrolled", count unchanged (R5)
  else course full
    CO --> RS : REJECTED("course full")
    RS --> S : rejection "course full", count unchanged (R5)
  else not enrolled and places left
    CO -> EN : create Enrollment(student, offeringId)
    activate EN
    EN --> CO : enrollment
    deactivate EN
    CO -> CO : countEnrollments increases by 1
    CO --> RS : CONFIRMED(enrollment)
    RS --> S : confirmation with enrollment details (R4)
  end
end

note over CO
  Atomic mechanism: the duplicate check,
  the capacity check, the decrement of
  availablePlaces, and the Enrollment
  creation run in one atomic transaction
  (row lock on the offering, or conditional
  update), so two concurrent requests for
  the last place cannot both succeed.
end note

deactivate CO
deactivate RS
@enduml